{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nTwo grounded code-review false negatives (escaped-bug deep-dive on cranial-goodly-seahog; user-approved design 2026-08-18, recorded verbatim in this ticket's comments) drove an approved three-part change set: citric-preregal-ladybird — a deletion-impact/api-compat finding naming the removed PUBLIC API `rebar.llm.review_ticket` plus a concrete broken external test scored impact 0.30, below the approved deletion-impact@0.60 / api-compat@0.51 blocking flips; brattish-ladyish-jaguar — a pass-2 recall failure on a workflow-YAML artifact. The approved set: (a1) churn/freq_mult amplify-only, never suppress, and never dampen a SERIOUS-tier binary; (a2) version-signal gating of `unversioned_published_contract_break`; (proposal-3) a pass-2 removed-public-symbol sub-question keyed on the EXPORT (not a cited caller) feeding a targeted impact boost.\n\nSTATUS OF a1: already landed on main by code-v4 (commit 61d50b0513, ticket 7f9f-05f4-796a-4c63): the debt-lane churn amplifier is [1.0,1.5] (amplify-only) and the serious-maint lane is undamped, pinned by tests/unit/test_impact_code.py (test_serious_maint_undamped_by_churn, test_debt_churn_zero_is_amplifier_one_not_half, test_freq_mult_cold_vs_hot). For a1 this ticket only corrects the stale \"churn 0 => freq_mult 0.5\" comment in workflow_ops.py.\n\n## Approach\nImplement a2 + proposal-3 on top of code-v4, each behavior change RED first (a test proving the current wrong score / missing gating) then GREEN:\n\n- a2 (pass-2 classification gating): redefine `unversioned_published_contract_break` in BOTH pass-2 surfaces — the pydantic field description (verify_models.py CodeSeverityAttrs) and the code-review-verify.md prompt bullet — as TRUE only when the published-contract break LACKS a version/deprecation signal (a major version bump, a deprecation cycle, or a CHANGELOG breaking-change entry); a MANAGED removal (any such signal present) is FALSE.\n- proposal-3 (pass-2 sub-question + deterministic boost): add two abstain-safe booleans to CodeSeverityAttrs — `removed_public_symbol` (TRUE when the finding cites a symbol this diff REMOVES whose name was reachable from the public API: `__all__`/re-export, a CLI command, or an MCP tool; detection keyed on the EXPORT, never on a cited caller — the absence of an internal caller does not prove an external API unused) and `version_signal_present` (TRUE when the removal carries one of the a2 signals). `decide.impact_code`'s serious-maint lane gains the derived contribution: `removed_public_symbol AND NOT version_signal_present` => the 0.9 unversioned-contract-break tier. Both fields default False, so an older/absent verifier ABSTAINS (no boost, never suppression); the boost is amplify-only — it can never lower an existing score. Bump sidecar IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION code-v4 -> code-v5 (impact semantics changed; sidecars segment by version), updating the exact-string version pins in tests.\n- Eval spec: add one fire case (unmanaged removal of an exported public symbol) and one no-fire case (managed removal with a deprecation cycle + CHANGELOG breaking-change entry) to code-review-verify.eval.yaml, offline-validated by the existing spec-discipline tests.\n- Interpretation note (recorded deliberately): the operator scope comment says the boost targets findings \"that cite a REMOVED public symbol together with a named broken caller\"; the user-approved design comment explicitly keys detection on the EXPORT, \"NOT on a cited caller\". The design comment wins — a named broken caller is NOT required for the boost. Assume this default unless the operator overrides it.\n\nThe pass-3 validity<0.5 hard-drop stays impact-blind, exactly as the approved design states (the brattish lever is pass-2 recall, addressed by the prompt/labeling changes above; no decider change here).\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify_models.py — a2-gated `unversioned_published_contract_break` description; 2 new CodeSeverityAttrs booleans\n- src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py — impact_code serious-maint boost path (code-v5)\n- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-verify.md — gated bullet + removed-public-symbol sub-question guidance\n- src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py — IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION \"code-v5\"\n- src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py — correct the stale freq_mult-0.5 comment (a1 residue)\n- src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-verify.eval.yaml — fire/no-fire removal dataset cases\n- tests/unit/test_impact_code.py — boost/abstain/managed-removal tests + the citric-preregal-ladybird replay\n- tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py — version pin -> code-v5\n- tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py — prompt/description text pins for a2 + proposal-3\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: `impact_code({\"removed_public_symbol\": True}) == 0.72` (0.9 serious tier x 0.8 non-silent amp) and the citric-preregal-ladybird replay attrs (capability_degraded + reachable_path_without_automated_coverage + trigger_likelihood rare + removed_public_symbol) score >= 0.60, clearing the deletion-impact@0.60 / api-compat@0.51 flips end-to-end through the packaged routing. Failure/edge paths: a managed removal (`version_signal_present: True`) gets NO boost and scores exactly as before the change; empty attrs still score 0.0 (abstain); `version_signal_present` alone changes nothing; the boost never lowers a score that other lanes already earned. Prompt/model text pins assert the version-signal gating and the export-keyed sub-question wording on both pass-2 surfaces. Offline eval-spec validation covers the new dataset cases. Proving command: `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_impact_code.py tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py tests/unit/test_code_review_evals.py tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `impact_code({\"removed_public_symbol\": True}) == 0.72` and the citric-preregal-ladybird replay scores >= 0.60 through the real packaged routing — checked by `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_impact_code.py`.\n- [ ] A managed removal never trips the boost: the same attrs with `version_signal_present: True` score exactly the pre-change value, and empty attrs still score 0.0 — checked by `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_impact_code.py`.\n- [ ] `unversioned_published_contract_break` is version-signal-gated on BOTH pass-2 surfaces (field description + prompt bullet name the major-bump / deprecation-cycle / CHANGELOG-breaking-change signals and the managed-removal=>FALSE rule) — checked by the text pins in `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py`.\n- [ ] The verify prompt carries the removed-public-symbol sub-question keyed on the EXPORT (`__all__`/re-export, CLI command, MCP tool), explicitly not on a cited caller — checked by the text pins in `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_code_review_ws2.py`.\n- [ ] IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION == \"code-v5\" and code-review-verify.eval.yaml gains one fire + one no-fire removal case that pass strict offline spec validation — checked by `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py tests/unit/test_code_review_evals.py`.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass in the worktree — checked by running them."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787349990941524001,"uuid":"f0403766-ca1a-4a54-a0af-7b41e84dbcc7"}